                 "These are the three traditional reef categories, not the only possible reef shapes; patch and platform reefs also occur. Reef construction requires successful settlement of coral larvae on firm surfaces, followed by long-term calcium-carbonate deposition. Reef position and shape reflect sea-level history, seafloor topography, sediment, waves, temperature and light. Do not label a single branching coral colony as an entire barrier reef.",
